NEEDS OWNER CONFIRMATION — do not treat this file as settled.

This is a conservative placeholder chosen because the repository contained no
license decision of any kind: no LICENSE file, no `license` key in package.json,
and no statement in any document. All-rights-reserved is the default that
applies to an unlicensed work anyway, so writing it down changes nothing legally
while making the position explicit.

Two things the owner should decide deliberately:

1. Whether the repository should stay PUBLIC. It is public today
   (github.com/fabrykjoh12/Hanzi-dojo), which is a fine choice — but it should
   be a chosen one, since the code, content pipeline and internal docs are all
   readable by anyone.

2. Whether all-rights-reserved is the intent, or whether an actual open-source
   license (MIT, Apache-2.0, AGPL-3.0, …) is wanted. That is a product decision
   with real consequences, and it was not made here.

Also unresolved, and tracked in docs/CONTENT-PROVENANCE-AUDIT.md: the origin of
the icon master `src/assets/86055582-d1d3-4cb7-a460-6c907025fe15.png`, from
which every shipped app icon derives. Until that is established, the copyright
line above should not be read as a claim over that mark.
